<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Kelgran says terminates talks with Kudu.</title>
<headline>Kelgran says terminates talks with Kudu.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African granite producer Kelgran Ltd on Friday said its controlling shareholder Malaysia's Mycom SA had terminated negotiations.</p>
<p>An earlier announcement said Kelgran was in talks with Kudu Granite, prompting speculation of a merger and the further consolidation of the country's granite sector following Kelgran's swallowing up of Ketter Granite Holdings in July.</p>
<p>Kudu is 56 percent held by Deutsche Steinindustrie. Mycom holds 57.4 percent of Kelgran.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
